"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide explains how to use the [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") to implement quantum algorithms directly in fermionic space, rather than mapping to qubits first.\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menerangkan cara menggunakan [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") untuk melaksanakan algoritma kuantum terus dalam ruang fermionik, dan bukannya memetakan kepada qubit terlebih dahulu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why use fermionic circuits {#why-use-fermionic-circuits}"
msgstr "Mengapa menggunakan litar fermionik {#why-use-fermionic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the traditional workflow for implementing the time evolution of a fermionic Hamiltonian on a qubit-based architecture:\n"
msgstr "Pertimbangkan aliran kerja tradisional untuk melaksanakan evolusi masa bagi Hamiltonian fermionik pada seni bina berasaskan qubit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the fermionic Hamiltonian (for example, $H = \\sum_{pq} h_{pq} c^\\dagger_p c_q$).\n"
msgstr "Takrifkan Hamiltonian fermionik (contohnya, $H = \\sum_{pq} h_{pq} c^\\dagger_p c_q$).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map it to a qubit operator (for example, by using the Jordan-Wigner mapping).\n"
msgstr "Petakannya kepada operator qubit (contohnya, dengan menggunakan pemetaan Jordan-Wigner).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implement the time evolution in qubit space (using Trotterization or other methods).\n"
msgstr "Laksanakan evolusi masa dalam ruang qubit (menggunakan Trotterization atau kaedah lain).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This approach has a fundamental limitation; early mapping to qubits discards problem-aware knowledge about the fermionic structure. Standard optimization passes cannot exploit fermionic symmetries or allowed term reorderings, resulting in suboptimal circuits with unnecessary depths and gate counts.\n"
msgstr "Pendekatan ini mempunyai had asas; pemetaan awal kepada qubit membuang pengetahuan yang peka masalah tentang struktur fermionik. Laluan pengoptimuman piawai tidak dapat mengeksploitasi simetri fermionik atau penyusunan semula sebutan yang dibenarkan, lalu menghasilkan litar yang tidak optimum dengan kedalaman dan bilangan Gate yang tidak perlu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") enables a better workflow:\n"
msgstr "[`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") membolehkan aliran kerja yang lebih baik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implement the time evolution directly in fermionic space using fermionic gates.\n"
msgstr "Laksanakan evolusi masa terus dalam ruang fermionik menggunakan Gate fermionik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map to qubit space as part of the transpilation process.\n"
msgstr "Petakan kepada ruang qubit sebagai sebahagian daripada proses transpilasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This approach addresses the limitation by keeping problem-aware knowledge in fermionic space, where optimization passes can exploit fermionic structure and commutation relations to reduce circuit depth. The fermionic circuit describes what computation to perform, while transpilation handles how to map it to qubits, providing a cleaner separation of concerns.\n"
msgstr "Pendekatan ini menangani had tersebut dengan mengekalkan pengetahuan yang peka masalah dalam ruang fermionik, di mana laluan pengoptimuman dapat mengeksploitasi struktur fermionik dan hubungan kekomutan untuk mengurangkan kedalaman litar. Litar fermionik menerangkan pengiraan apa yang perlu dilakukan, manakala transpilasi mengendalikan cara memetakannya kepada qubit, sekali gus memberikan pengasingan tanggungjawab yang lebih kemas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generic mode indexing {#generic-mode-indexing}"
msgstr "Pengindeksan mod generik {#generic-mode-indexing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both the [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") module and the [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") use generic mode-based indexing that makes no assumptions about the nature of the modes. A mode is simply an abstract index labeling a fermionic degree of freedom, with no inherent semantics. This design choice mirrors the operators module and ensures maximum flexibility. For example, you can implement time evolution for any operator implementing the [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol, regardless of its mathematical representation.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua modul [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") dan [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") menggunakan pengindeksan berasaskan mod generik yang tidak membuat andaian tentang sifat mod tersebut. Mod hanyalah indeks abstrak yang melabelkan satu darjah kebebasan fermionik, tanpa semantik yang wujud. Pilihan reka bentuk ini mencerminkan modul operators dan memastikan fleksibiliti maksimum. Sebagai contoh, anda boleh melaksanakan evolusi masa bagi sebarang operator yang melaksanakan protokol [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\"), tanpa mengira perwakilan matematiknya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a fermionic circuit {#build-a-fermionic-circuit}"
msgstr "Bina litar fermionik {#build-a-fermionic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example below implements the time evolution described in the previous section. It constructs a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") by specifying the number of fermionic modes, then adds fermionic gates from the [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") to implement the time evolution.\n"
msgstr "Contoh di bawah melaksanakan evolusi masa yang diterangkan dalam bahagian sebelumnya. Ia membina [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") dengan menentukan bilangan mod fermionik, kemudian menambah Gate fermionik daripada [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") untuk melaksanakan evolusi masa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example also demonstrates how to incorporate domain knowledge into an operator by using [operator term grouping](grouping#grouping-explanation). By assigning group indices to the Hamiltonian terms, you preserve structural information that optimization passes can exploit throughout the transpilation stack.\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini juga menunjukkan cara menerapkan pengetahuan domain ke dalam operator dengan menggunakan [pengumpulan sebutan operator](grouping#grouping-explanation). Dengan menetapkan indeks kumpulan kepada sebutan Hamiltonian, anda mengekalkan maklumat struktur yang dapat dieksploitasi oleh laluan pengoptimuman sepanjang tindanan transpilasi.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A simple \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a single time evolution gate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-2.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A simple \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a single time evolution gate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-2.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A decomposed \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with several time evolution gates.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-3.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A decomposed \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with several time evolution gates.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-3.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notice how the operator term grouping is preserved even in simple operations like decomposition. This demonstrates how structural information flows through the circuit stack. To understand the full transpilation to qubits, refer to the [Transpiling fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guide.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bagaimana pengumpulan sebutan operator dikekalkan walaupun dalam operasi mudah seperti penguraian. Ini menunjukkan bagaimana maklumat struktur mengalir melalui tindanan litar. Untuk memahami transpilasi penuh kepada qubit, rujuk panduan [Transpilasi litar fermionik](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep gates apart with a barrier {#keep-gates-apart-with-a-barrier}"
msgstr "Pisahkan Gate dengan penghalang {#keep-gates-apart-with-a-barrier}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The optimization passes fuse neighboring gates where they can. For example, [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") combines a run of consecutive [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates into one, and [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") folds an [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") into the rotation that follows it.\n"
msgstr "Laluan pengoptimuman menggabungkan Gate yang berjiran jika boleh. Sebagai contoh, [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") menggabungkan satu jujukan Gate [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") berturutan menjadi satu, dan [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") melipat [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") ke dalam putaran yang mengikutinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use [`FermionicCircuit.barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") when you want to prevent that. A barrier carries no unitary effect, so it does not change the state your circuit prepares; it only marks a point that the passes do not fuse across. Call it without arguments to span every mode, or pass the modes to restrict it to:\n"
msgstr "Gunakan [`FermionicCircuit.barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") apabila anda ingin menghalangnya. Penghalang tidak membawa kesan unitari, jadi ia tidak mengubah keadaan yang disediakan oleh litar anda; ia hanya menandakan satu titik yang tidak dilintasi penggabungan oleh laluan tersebut. Panggil tanpa argumen untuk merangkumi setiap mod, atau luluskan mod untuk mengehadkannya kepada:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a barrier separating two orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-5.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a barrier separating two orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-5.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Barriers survive the fermion-to-qubit transpilation, so they also constrain the qubit-level optimization that follows. The [Transpile fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guide covers that stage.\n"
msgstr "Penghalang kekal semasa transpilasi fermion-ke-qubit, jadi ia turut mengekang pengoptimuman peringkat qubit yang menyusul. Panduan [Transpilasi litar fermionik](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) membincangkan peringkat tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat a circuit {#repeat-a-circuit}"
msgstr "Ulang litar {#repeat-a-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many algorithms apply the same block of gates many times over. Time evolution is the common case: a Trotter step is built once, then repeated to reach the target time. Use [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") to build the repeated circuit, and [`compose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose\") to join it to a state preparation prefix.\n"
msgstr "Banyak algoritma menggunakan blok Gate yang sama berkali-kali. Evolusi masa ialah kes biasa: satu langkah Trotter dibina sekali, kemudian diulang untuk mencapai masa sasaran. Gunakan [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") untuk membina litar yang diulang, dan [`compose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose\") untuk menyambungkannya kepada awalan penyediaan keadaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example below builds a second-order Trotter step for a Fermi-Hubbard model. The step is symmetric: it splits the hopping term into two half-duration [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates surrounding the on-site interaction.\n"
msgstr "Contoh di bawah membina langkah Trotter peringkat kedua untuk model Fermi-Hubbard. Langkah ini simetri: ia memecahkan sebutan lompatan kepada dua Gate [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") berdurasi separuh yang mengapit interaksi tapak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeating the step and composing it onto a Hartree-Fock reference gives the full evolution:\n"
msgstr "Mengulang langkah tersebut dan menggubahnya pada rujukan Hartree-Fock memberikan evolusi penuh:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-8.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The repetitions are flattened into the returned circuit rather than wrapped in a single gate, so [`count_ops()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops\") counts two rotations per step. That flattening is what makes the redundancy at the step boundaries visible to the transpiler: the trailing half-duration rotation of one step and the leading one of the next are adjacent, so [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") combines them into a single rotation.\n"
msgstr "Ulangan diratakan ke dalam litar yang dikembalikan dan bukannya dibungkus dalam satu Gate, jadi [`count_ops()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops\") mengira dua putaran bagi setiap langkah. Perataan itulah yang menjadikan lebihan pada sempadan langkah kelihatan kepada Transpiler: putaran berdurasi separuh di hujung satu langkah dan yang di permulaan langkah seterusnya bersebelahan, jadi [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") menggabungkannya menjadi satu putaran.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps and merged orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-10.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps and merged orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-10.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result costs one rotation per step plus one, which is what you get by fusing those half-steps by hand. Writing the step in its natural symmetric form and repeating it produces the same circuit, so the fusion is left to the optimization stage.\n"
msgstr "Hasilnya berkos satu putaran bagi setiap langkah ditambah satu, iaitu apa yang anda peroleh dengan menggabungkan separuh langkah tersebut secara manual. Menulis langkah dalam bentuk simetri semula jadinya dan mengulanginya menghasilkan litar yang sama, jadi penggabungan diserahkan kepada peringkat pengoptimuman.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you need the repetitions kept apart, pass `insert_barriers=True` to place a [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") between them. The optimization passes do not fuse gates across a barrier, so every rotation survives:\n"
msgstr "Apabila anda memerlukan ulangan diasingkan, luluskan `insert_barriers=True` untuk meletakkan [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") di antaranya. Laluan pengoptimuman tidak menggabungkan Gate merentasi penghalang, jadi setiap putaran kekal:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps separated by barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-12.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps separated by barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-12.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The `reps` argument of [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") is a different concept. It subdivides a single [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate into more, shorter factors, whereas [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") duplicates whole circuits. Repeating a circuit that holds one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") only multiplies its total evolution time.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Argumen `reps` bagi [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") ialah konsep yang berbeza. Ia membahagikan satu Gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") kepada lebih banyak faktor yang lebih pendek, manakala [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") menggandakan litar keseluruhan. Mengulang litar yang mengandungi satu [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") hanya mendarabkan jumlah masa evolusinya.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure fermionic modes {#measure-fermionic-modes}"
msgstr "Ukur mod fermionik {#measure-fermionic-modes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\") reads every mode out into a classical bit of its own, pairing mode `i` with bit `i`. Use [`measure()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure\") with your own [`ClassicalRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.ClassicalRegister) to read out only some of them.\n"
msgstr "[`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\") membaca setiap mod ke dalam bit klasik tersendiri, memasangkan mod `i` dengan bit `i`. Gunakan [`measure()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure\") dengan [`ClassicalRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.ClassicalRegister) anda sendiri untuk membaca hanya sebahagian daripadanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Passing `inplace=False` returns a measured copy and leaves the original alone, which matters because a measurement is not unitary: a circuit carrying one can no longer be applied to a state vector, so keep an unmeasured circuit around if you also want to simulate it.\n"
msgstr "Melulus `inplace=False` mengembalikan salinan yang diukur dan membiarkan yang asal, yang penting kerana pengukuran tidak unitari: litar yang membawanya tidak lagi boleh dikenakan pada vektor keadaan, jadi simpan litar yang tidak diukur jika anda juga ingin mensimulasikannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measuring here, rather than on the transpiled [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit), is what keeps the sampled bitstrings easy to read. A fermionic measurement names the mode it reads, so every stage that moves modes around ([`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") at the fermionic level, layout and routing at the qubit level) carries the measurement along with it, and the bitstring stays indexed by the mode you asked about.\n"
msgstr "Mengukur di sini, dan bukannya pada [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) yang telah ditranspil, menjadikan rentetan bit yang disampel mudah dibaca. Pengukuran fermionik menamakan mod yang dibacanya, jadi setiap peringkat yang mengalihkan mod ([`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") pada peringkat fermionik, susun atur dan penghalaan pada peringkat qubit) membawa pengukuran bersamanya, dan rentetan bit kekal diindeks mengikut mod yang anda tanyakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Unlike [`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#measure_all), no [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") is inserted before the measurements. Call [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") yourself first if you want one there.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Tidak seperti [`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#measure_all), tiada [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") disisipkan sebelum pengukuran. Panggil [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") sendiri terlebih dahulu jika anda mahukannya di situ.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Whether a measured bit means what you expect depends on the fermion-to-qubit encoding, which is chosen during transpilation rather than here. Under an occupation-basis encoding such as Jordan-Wigner each mode is carried by one qubit and the bit is that mode’s occupation; see [`FermionicMeasure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-fermionic-measure#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Sama ada bit yang diukur bermaksud seperti yang anda jangkakan bergantung pada pengekodan fermion-ke-qubit, yang dipilih semasa transpilasi dan bukan di sini. Di bawah pengekodan berasaskan asas penghunian seperti Jordan-Wigner, setiap mod dibawa oleh satu qubit dan bit tersebut ialah penghunian mod itu; lihat [`FermionicMeasure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-fermionic-measure#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile fermionic circuits {#transpile-fermionic-circuits}"
msgstr "Transpilasi litar fermionik {#transpile-fermionic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To implement the quantum algorithm represented by your [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") it must be transpiled to a [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). You can learn how to do this in the [Transpile fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guide.\n"
msgstr "Untuk melaksanakan algoritma kuantum yang diwakili oleh [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") anda, ia mesti ditranspil kepada [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). Anda boleh mempelajari cara melakukannya dalam panduan [Transpilasi litar fermionik](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"

